-- statement:
--   For a finite coordinate type with decidable equality and natural side lengths, let a finite bad set lie inside the natural box. If real functions $F,G$ agree outside that bad set within the box and satisfy $|F-G|\le1$ on the box, their box means differ by at most the bad-set cardinality divided by the box volume.
